## Lore

Subject to much controversy within the Coalition States, feared and respected by
most others, the Glitter Boy pilots of Free Quebec have become legendary heroes
in their own right. Scrutinised and politically attacked by Chi-Town for
decades, they have come to symbolise rebellious patriots who stand for Free
Quebec and against all who oppose her, Emperor Prosek and the Coalition States
included. That, their teamwork and their famous power armor has made them the
elite among the fighting forces of the Quebec Military and patriotic heroes in
the public eye.

The most illustrious pilots trace their lineage as far back as ten generations,
roughly 200 to 250 years, and some claim descent from the original 288 Quebec
pilots of legend. For these men and women, being a Glitter Boy pilot is a matter
of tradition and tremendous prestige. They are the elite of the elite, and most
get special privileges, officer''s training and recognition; a full half of all
commissioned officers in the Glitter Boy Legions are said to have descended from
these historic families.

Roughly one third are female. They are highly motivated, loyal and disciplined
soldiers dedicated to their country, and they rarely hot shot or defy orders.

## GM Notes

Average level of experience for an NPC is 1D4+4, and high ranking officers are
1D4+6. **Glitter Boy pilots who are NOT among the Descended range at 1D4+2** ' || char(8212) || '
they are the same trade without the lineage.

Average rank: starts as a 2nd Lieutenant, with experienced officers averaging
Colonel. Known as the "Officers of Generations" and "The Descended". Currently
70% of Quebec Glitter Boy pilots are Descended.

**This is a different class from the freelance Glitter Boy of the Rifts RPG**,
and the book says so directly: these professional soldiers have different
training. It also gives the independent version a lineage option ' || char(8212) || ' a
"Descended Independent" gets +1 on initiative, +1 to strike, +2 to pull punch,
+3 to save vs Horror Factor, +20 S.D.C. and +1 additional melee attack when
using a GB, but only with a long family tradition rather than a recently
acquired suit. That option belongs to the `glitter-boy` class and is not applied
here.

An individual or pair of Taurus Glitter Boys is usually assigned a Reload Team
and a Side Kick. Most Glitter Boy squads of 6-10 members are assigned 2-4 Side
Kicks and one Reload Team; squads on covert or intelligence-gathering missions
may have anywhere from none to one Side Kick each, and no Reload Team.

The soldier''s quarters is a small apartment, typically in the same building as
their teammates: living room, bathroom with tub and shower, study, kitchenette
and bedroom, with a CD stereo, television and VCD, mini-refrigerator, basic
furniture and a comfortable bed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
